From cc1547c4be98fb2ba7daf4c2345e20f6abcbec36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <contact@buildthings.co>
Date: Mon, 05 Oct 2026 13:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash family for two DGX Sparks (TP=2, EXL3
 2.9 bpw)

families/deepseek_v41/: a CUDA engine for the MiaAI-Lab EXL3 2.9 bpw packs of
DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash over two DGX Sparks: CSA2 attention with FP8 KV rows and the
lightning indexer, Single-Pass mHC, Engram rows read from packed per-rank NVMe shards,
the routed experts on EXL3 kernels for GB10 (x3ld / x3seg / x3gm), exact DSpark
speculative decoding (drafted replies == serial replies), CED bounded-replay prefill,
a 4-slot batcher with a shared FP8 pool, sessions with an NVMe tier, prepared per-rank
folders for fast restarts, structured output, DSML tool calls, and an OpenAI API.

Host memory in long prefills (hostmem.py, G12): a segment's Engram rows live in reused
NumPy-owned buffers, not torch's CPU allocator (its embedded mimalloc kept frees made on
another thread); NumPy's transparent-huge-page request is off on the ranks; the Engram
hash memo is bounded by the rows it holds; TF_DSV41_MEMPROBE diagnostics. A round stall
watchdog (stall.py, TF_DSV41_STALL_S) and deadlines on Engram reads
(TF_DSV41_ENGRAM_WAIT_S). RoPE tables built in fixed blocks, so an entry no longer
depends on the table's length (prefill bits independent of the segment split). DSpark
self-distillation tooling (dsparkdata / dsparktrain / dsparkdelta,
TF_DSV41_DSPARK_DELTA, off by default).

Decode rewrites (G13), each behind a lever that defaults to 0 and gives the same bits
on or off: the mHC boundary of a decode window as one CUDA launch (mhc_cuda,
TF_DSV41_MHC_CUDA); CSA2's decode attention core and the indexer's top-k in CUDA
(csa2/attn_cuda, topk_cuda, TF_DSV41_ATTN_CUDA); the dense EXL3 linears over a
16-byte-coalesced repack of the trellis (dense3, TF_DSV41_DENSE_V3); the decode MoE chain
shortened (moe_fused, TF_DSV41_MOE_FUSED); the CSA2 indexer / compressor on a side
stream inside the window graph (branches, TF_DSV41_BRANCHES). CPU emulators, compile
tests and GPU tests for each.

Window levers (G14), bit for bit, defaults unchanged: the round plan through a RoCE host
mailbox (planlink, TF_DSV41_PLAN_LINK=rdma, roce_msg.h) with pinned plan threads
(TF_DSV41_PLAN_PIN); L2 prefetch paced beside the exchanges (l2pace, TF_DSV41_L2PF_PACE_GBPS);
a shorter critical path in the RoCE all-gather kernel (GLM53_TF_ROCE_FAST) and the exchange
split tools (roce_bench, roce_split); BRANCHES on prioritised streams; calibration VERSION 4
(every verify row measured). Image input (G15-G16, TF_DSV41_IMAGES=placeholder | reject |
native): DeepSeek's ViT + aligner on rank 0, the image span, gate.bias_vl routing, Engram
shut at image positions; the vision Store counts a table's references once per image (one
image twice in a request no longer kills both ranks). The expert map (TF_DSV41_XMAP) and
joint depth mode 2, off.

Serving memory (G16-G19): an LRU graph cache (TF_DSV41_GRAPHS_MAX 48) with context buckets
1.25x apart past 32K, one eviction a memory dip and capture refusals in prefill dips
deferred (TF_DSV41_GRAPH_DIP_ROUNDS); host trims off the round thread; the NVMe session
tier's index keeps (length, chain, tail), not every entry's ids; fail fast on both ranks
(failfast.py, TF_DSV41_FAILFAST=1: a failure in either rank's round ends the pair in ~1 s
with exit 70); a two-rank admission floor that prices a prompt's prefill transient
(TF_DSV41_FLOOR_PRICE=1, rank 1's memory over the plan link's TCP connection); adaptive
prefill rows from the tighter rank's memory (TF_DSV41_PREFILL_ADAPT=1). An opt-in
allocator ceiling (TF_DSV41_ALLOC_CEIL_GIB) and GIL switch interval (TF_DSV41_SWITCH_MS),
both off.

Prefill levers (G16-G17), the same bits on or off: one prefill weight copy
(TF_DSV41_PF_COPIES), the mHC prefill kernel (TF_DSV41_MHC_PF), the dense EXL3 prefill
GEMM with the trellis decoded inside it and a tuned tile table (pfdense,
TF_DSV41_PF_DENSE=fused, TF_DSV41_PF_DENSE_TABLE), full-mode prefill with the decoder over
its dependency cone (TF_DSV41_FULL_CONE), and, off: TF_DSV41_PF_XOVL, TF_DSV41_PREFILL_TILES,
4,096-row windows (refused at boot without TF_DSV41_PF_4K_MEMORY_OK=1),
TF_DSV41_SPEC_NUCLEUS. m2bench: steady aggregates, same-workload and distinct-prompt cells,
per-stream reply digests (--c-exact), --prefill-reply.

Geometric context buckets, the allocator ceiling, the switch interval and failing fast
across ranks are ideas from bertholomus/TensorFold (deepseek-v41-tp2, Apache-2.0),
re-implemented here (THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).

Packaging: deepseek_v41/cuda/csa2's CUDA sources and the pfdense headers are package
data (an installed tree could not build ATTN_CUDA or PF_DENSE=fused).

Also: the EXL3 linear's device-side skip (graph-safe), fp64 in the communicator's
dtype table, --kv-dtype fp8, extra model ids in /v1/models, the family's tests.

MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Jay Leaton (NOTICE, THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md). No
draft-vocabulary ranking is shipped for TF_DSV41_DRAFT_HEAD=trim (off by default).
